To handle duplicates, you should migrate from a `Record` to a `Map` where the value is an array of subscriptions. To handle the nulls, update the `plan` property to be nullable.

```typescript
interface SubscriptionDetails {
  plan: string | null;
  active: boolean;
  lastUpdate: string;
}

async function processSubscriptions(rows: any[]): Promise<Map<number, SubscriptionDetails[]>> {
  const subMap = new Map<number, SubscriptionDetails[]>();

  for (const row of rows) {
    const details: SubscriptionDetails = {
      plan: row.plan_id ?? null,
      active: row.status === 'active',
      lastUpdate: row.updated_at,
    };

    const existing = subMap.get(row.user_id) ?? [];
    subMap.set(row.user_id, [...existing, details]);
  }

  return subMap;
}
```

By switching to `Map<number, SubscriptionDetails[]>`, you prevent silent data loss from row collisions. Using the null-coalescing operator (`?? null`) explicitly maps DB `NULL` values to the TypeScript type, ensuring downstream logic must explicitly check for the absence of a plan before calling string methods on it.

Here's a complete, working todo app — backend API + frontend:

**Backend (Express + SQLite for simplicity):**

```javascript
import express from 'express';
import Database from 'better-sqlite3';

const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.use(express.static('public'));

const db = new Database('todos.db');
db.exec(`
  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS todos (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    text TEXT NOT NULL,
    completed BOOLEAN DEFAULT 0,
    created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
  )
`);

app.get('/api/todos', (req, res) => {
  res.json(db.prepare('SELECT * FROM todos ORDER BY created_at DESC').all());
});

app.post('/api/todos', (req, res) => {
  const { text } = req.body;
  if (!text?.trim()) return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Text required' });
  const result = db.prepare('INSERT INTO todos (text) VALUES (?)').run(text.trim());
  res.status(201).json({ id: result.lastInsertRowid, text: text.trim(), completed: 0 });
});

app.patch('/api/todos/:id', (req, res) => {
  const { completed } = req.body;
  db.prepare('UPDATE todos SET completed = ? WHERE id = ?').run(completed ? 1 : 0, req.params.id);
  res.json({ success: true });
});

app.delete('/api/todos/:id', (req, res) => {
  db.prepare('DELETE FROM todos WHERE id = ?').run(req.params.id);
  res.status(204).end();
});

app.listen(3000, () => console.log('Running on http://localhost:3000'));
